# VIAME's python dependencies: everything a default build needs.
#
# This file and its siblings replace the lists that were computed by
# `cmake/add_project_python_deps.cmake`, where a dependency's version bounds
# were spread across a dozen `if()` branches and could only be read by
# configuring. A requirement file can say the same thing in the form pip
# already understands, including the python-version bounds, which are
# environment markers here rather than branches.
#
# `*.lock` beside this file is what the build installs: the fully pinned
# resolution of these, one per (python, accelerator) variant, produced by
# `pip-compile`. Edit the `.in`, recompile the `.lock`, commit both.
#
# Extras that are not part of a default build have their own file and pull
# this one in: `cuda12.in`, `cuda13.in` and `cpu.in` choose the accelerator,
# and `learn.in`, `colmap.in` and `test.in` follow the `VIAME_ENABLE_*`
# option of the same name. An extra's lock is compiled with its
# accelerator's lock as a constraint, so the two agree on every shared pin
# and `pip install -r cuda12.lock -r colmap.lock` is coherent.

# --- build helpers -----------------------------------------------------------
ordered_set
build
cython
# >=75.3.0 for the builtin bdist_wheel (added in 70.1.0); without a lower
# bound an old pip counts the distro's 59.x as satisfying it and skips the
# upgrade. <76 because 76.0 removed `pkg_resources.get_distribution`, which
# imgaug, mmcv and others still build against.
setuptools>=75.3.0,<76
wheel>=0.45.0
scikit-build

